# determinism-repeat-permute — the draft-decide-run graph (two source gates,
# two egress paths). This vector pins SPEC §7.5 determinism two ways a runner
# can check: (1) repeating the same activations against this file MUST yield
# identical per-gate verdicts, master decisions and log traces every time
# (`repeat` in transport.json; rule 1); (2) running the same activations
# against `permutations/reordered.lg` — the same policy with its declarations
# textually reordered — MUST yield the same per-gate verdicts and master
# decisions (rule 2). Each activation reaches a single gate, so the pipe
# relation over the activated gates admits one topological order and the
# log is also the same (rule 3); contrast determinism-topo-tie, where the
# log follows the §7.4 tie-break for each declaration order. A determinism
# vector carries no expected.json: reordering declarations changes the
# declaration-order-dependent parts of the static observation by
# construction (SPEC §9, Order), so only the dynamic result
# (verdict/master/log) is compared — see conformance/README.md.
actor  bot7
human  alice  role legal
gate   draft   risk low    grant bot7
gate   decide  risk high   grant bot7
reserve automated_decision by legal when risk >= high
cord bot7   -> draft
cord bot7   -> decide
cord draft  -> master
cord decide -> master
